[2026/05/15 20:50:39] [DEBUG] isgsa.backend/openai: [cyan]Raw func call response: Choice(finish_reason='tool_calls', index=0, logprobs=None, message=ChatCompletionMessage(content=None, refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=[], audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=[ChatCompletionMessageFunctionToolCall(id='call_mrFGO3zeDH3BhtrTdxkxprfD', function=Function(arguments='{"nl_text":"We will build a compact LensKit 0.14.4 experiment script that loads the three provided raw files, applies 5-core filtering, binarizes MovieLens and Amazon interactions at rating > 3, and converts all datasets into implicit feedback. The script will generate five random seeds, perform a user-based 80/20 holdout split for each seed, train ALS, ItemKNN, and Pop with standard LensKit hyperparameters, and evaluate nDCG@1/5/10 and Precision@1/5/10 on the held-out users. I will keep the implementation simple and reproducible, using LensKit’s data structures and recommenders as much as possible, while adding small compatibility helpers if the exact API differs across submodules. The code will save all metrics arrays and intermediate results into the working directory with np.save, and it will also produce a few lightweight plots summarizing mean performance and seed sensitivity. For the statistical analysis, the script will compute per-seed metric tables, aggregate mean/std across seeds, and run a short paired comparison across seeds between algorithms to highlight whether split randomness is larger than model differences. Because the task is about split-seed sensitivity rather than tuning, I will not do hyperparameter search; instead I’ll rely on default or standard LensKit settings. The script will print a concise results table plus basic significance-style summaries so the experiment can be run end-to-end in one pass.","code":"import os\\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\\n\\nimport warnings\\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\'ignore\')\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport pandas as pd\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nfrom scipy import stats\\n\\n# LensKit imports (with compatibility fallbacks)\\ntry:\\n    from lenskit.algorithms.basic import Pop\\nexcept Exception:\\n    from lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular as Pop\\ntry:\\n    from lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF as ALS\\nexcept Exception:\\n    try:\\n        from lenskit.algorithms.als import BiasedMF as ALS\\n    except Exception:\\n        ALS = None\\ntry:\\n    from lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemItem as ItemKNN\\nexcept Exception:\\n    try:\\n        from lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemKNN\\n    except Exception:\\n        ItemKNN = None\\n\\nfrom lenskit import topn\\ntry:\\n    from lenskit.batch import predict_ranking\\nexcept Exception:\\n    predict_ranking = None\\n\\nexperiment_data = {\\n    \'MovieLens100K\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': [], \'timestamps\': []},\\n    \'AmazonVideoGames\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': [], \'timestamps\': []},\\n    \'LastFM\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': [], \'timestamps\': []},\\n}\\n\\ndef load_movielens(path=\'u.data\'):\\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\\\t\', names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'])\\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3].copy()\\n    return df[[\'user\', \'item\', \'timestamp\']]\\n\\ndef load_amazon(path=\'VideoGames.csv\'):\\n    df = pd.read_csv(path)\\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\\n    u = cols.get(\'user_id\', cols.get(\'reviewerid\', list(df.columns)[0]))\\n    i = cols.get(\'item_id\', cols.get(\'asin\', list(df.columns)[1]))\\n    r = cols.get(\'rating\', cols.get(\'overall\', list(df.columns)[2]))\\n    t = cols.get(\'timestamp\', cols.get(\'unixreviewtime\', None))\\n    df = df[df[r] > 3].copy()\\n    if t is None:\\n        df[\'timestamp\'] = np.arange(len(df))\\n        t = \'timestamp\'\\n    return df[[u, i, t]].rename(columns={u: \'user\', i: \'item\', t: \'timestamp\'})\\n\\ndef load_lastfm(path=\'user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat\'):\\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\\\t\')\\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\\n    u = cols.get(\'userID\'.lower(), cols.get(\'user_id\', list(df.columns)[0]))\\n    i = cols.get(\'artistID\'.lower(), cols.get(\'item_id\', list(df.columns)[1]))\\n    t = cols.get(\'timestamp\', list(df.columns)[-1])\\n    return df[[u, i, t]].rename(columns={u: \'user\', i: \'item\', t: \'timestamp\'})\\n\\ndef five_core(df):\\n    changed = True\\n    while changed:\\n        changed = False\\n        uc = df[\'user\'].value_counts()\\n        ic = df[\'item\'].value_counts()\\n        keep = df[\'user\'].isin(uc[uc >= 5].index) & df[\'item\'].isin(ic[ic >= 5].index)\\n        if keep.sum() != len(df):\\n            df = df[keep].copy()\\n            changed = True\\n    return df.reset_index(drop=True)\\n\\ndef remap_ids(df):\\n    u_map = {u: idx for idx, u in enumerate(df[\'user\'].unique())}\\n    i_map = {i: idx for idx, i in enumerate(df[\'item\'].unique())}\\n    out = df.copy()\\n    out[\'user\'] = out[\'user\'].map(u_map).astype(np.int32)\\n    out[\'item\'] = out[\'item\'].map(i_map).astype(np.int32)\\n    return out, u_map, i_map\\n\\ndef user_holdout_split(df, seed=42, frac=0.2):\\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n    test_idx = []\\n    for u, g in df.groupby(\'user\'):\\n        idx = g.index.to_numpy()\\n        n = max(1, int(np.ceil(len(idx) * frac)))\\n        test_idx.extend(rng.choice(idx, size=n, replace=False).tolist())\\n    test_idx = np.array(sorted(set(test_idx)))\\n    test = df.loc[test_idx].copy()\\n    train = df.drop(test_idx).copy()\\n    return train, test\\n\\ndef build_algo(name):\\n    if name == \'Pop\':\\n        return Pop()\\n    if name == \'ALS\':\\n        if ALS is None:\\n            raise RuntimeError(\'ALS not available in installed LensKit\')\\n        try:\\n            return ALS(features=50, iterations=15, reg=0.1, method=\'lu\')\\n        except Exception:\\n            try:\\n                return ALS(50, 15, 0.1)\\n            except Exception:\\n                return ALS()\\n    if name == \'ItemKNN\':\\n        if ItemKNN is None:\\n            raise RuntimeError(\'ItemKNN not available in installed LensKit\')\\n        try:\\n            return ItemKNN(nnbrs=40)\\n        except Exception:\\n            try:\\n                return ItemKNN(k=40)\\n            except Exception:\\n                return ItemKNN()\\n    raise ValueError(name)\\n\\ndef recs_for_users(algo, train, users, n=10):\\n    recs = []\\n    try:\\n        algo.fit(train)\\n    except Exception:\\n        algo.fit(train[[\'user\', \'item\']])\\n    for u in users:\\n        seen = train.loc[train[\'user\'] == u, \'item\'].tolist()\\n        try:\\n            rs = topn.make_recommendations(algo, [u], n=n, users=train[\'user\'].unique(), items=train[\'item\'].unique())\\n        except Exception:\\n            rs = None\\n        if rs is None:\\n            cand = pd.DataFrame({\'user\': [u] * len(train[\'item\'].unique()), \'item\': train[\'item\'].unique()})\\n            try:\\n                preds = algo.predict(cand)\\n                if isinstance(preds, pd.Series):\\n                    cand[\'score\'] = preds.values\\n                else:\\n                    cand[\'score\'] = np.asarray(preds)\\n            except Exception:\\n                scores = []\\n                for i in train[\'item\'].unique():\\n                    try:\\n                        s = algo.predict_for_user(u, i)\\n                    except Exception:\\n                        s = 0.0\\n                    scores.append(s)\\n                cand[\'score\'] = scores\\n        