[2026/05/15 20:51:26] [DEBUG] isgsa.backend/openai: [cyan]Raw func call response: Choice(finish_reason='tool_calls', index=0, logprobs=None, message=ChatCompletionMessage(content=None, refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=[], audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=[ChatCompletionMessageFunctionToolCall(id='call_jLXjfSTt87xSn7YmKojTMzIq', function=Function(arguments='{"nl_text":"I’ll build a single self-contained script that loads each raw file from the working directory, applies 5-core filtering, and converts MovieLens and Amazon ratings to implicit feedback using a >3 threshold. The script will then construct user-based 80/20 holdout splits for five fixed random seeds, train LensKit 0.14.4 models for ALS, ItemKNN, and Pop with default-style hyperparameters, and evaluate nDCG@k and Precision@k for k=1, 5, and 10. I’ll store per-seed metrics and other plottable outputs in a structured numpy-saveable dictionary, and also save summary tables and any figures to the working directory. For analysis, the code will compute mean and standard deviation across seeds and run a short paired statistical comparison across algorithms for each dataset/metric. To keep it robust, I’ll include lightweight preprocessing for the three different raw formats, ensure only implicit interactions are passed to the recommenders, and make the evaluation path compatible with LensKit’s APIs as much as possible. The script will print progress, including validation-style tracking per split if a validation step is used, and finish by writing the experiment_data.npy file and a compact CSV/NPY summary. The implementation will be intentionally simple and reproducible so it can serve as a baseline for later experiments.","code":"import os\\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\\n\\nimport warnings\\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\'ignore\')\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport pandas as pd\\nfrom scipy import stats\\nfrom collections import defaultdict\\nfrom sklearn.metrics import ndcg_score\\n\\nimport lenskit\\nfrom lenskit.data import SparseMatrix\\nfrom lenskit.batch import recommend\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import BiasedMF\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemItem\\n\\n# -----------------------\\n# Config\\n# -----------------------\\nseeds = [11, 22, 33, 44, 55]\\nks = [1, 5, 10]\\ndatasets = {\\n    \'MovieLens100K\': {\'path\': \'u.data\', \'sep\': \'\\\\t\', \'names\': [\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'], \'movie\': True},\\n    \'AmazonVideoGames\': {\'path\': \'VideoGames.csv\', \'sep\': \',\', \'names\': None, \'movie\': False},\\n    \'LastFM\': {\'path\': \'user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat\', \'sep\': \'\\\\t\', \'names\': None, \'movie\': False},\\n}\\nalg_names = [\'ALS\', \'ItemKNN\', \'Pop\']\\n\\nexperiment_data = {}\\nfor d in datasets:\\n    experiment_data[d] = {\\n        \'metrics\': {\'ndcg\': [], \'precision\': []},\\n        \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []},\\n        \'predictions\': [],\\n        \'ground_truth\': [],\\n        \'per_seed\': [],\\n    }\\n\\n# -----------------------\\n# Helpers\\n# -----------------------\\ndef load_dataset(name, cfg):\\n    p = cfg[\'path\']\\n    if not os.path.exists(p):\\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\'Missing {p}\')\\n    if name == \'MovieLens100K\':\\n        df = pd.read_csv(p, sep=\'\\\\t\', names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'], engine=\'python\')\\n        df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3].copy()\\n        df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\\n    elif name == \'AmazonVideoGames\':\\n        df = pd.read_csv(p)\\n        cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\\n        ucol = cols.get(\'user_id\') or cols.get(\'reviewerid\') or cols.get(\'user\')\\n        icol = cols.get(\'item_id\') or cols.get(\'asin\') or cols.get(\'item\')\\n        rcol = cols.get(\'rating\') or cols.get(\'overall\')\\n        if ucol is None or icol is None:\\n            raise ValueError(\'Could not identify user/item columns in Amazon data\')\\n        if rcol is None:\\n            df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\\n        else:\\n            df = df[df[rcol] > 3].copy()\\n            df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\\n        df = df.rename(columns={ucol: \'user\', icol: \'item\'})\\n        df[\'timestamp\'] = np.arange(len(df))\\n    elif name == \'LastFM\':\\n        df = pd.read_csv(p, sep=\'\\\\t\')\\n        cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\\n        ucol = cols.get(\'user_id\') or cols.get(\'user\')\\n        icol = cols.get(\'artist_id\') or cols.get(\'item_id\') or cols.get(\'artist\')\\n        if ucol is None or icol is None:\\n            raise ValueError(\'Could not identify user/item columns in LastFM data\')\\n        df = df.rename(columns={ucol: \'user\', icol: \'item\'})\\n        if \'weight\' in cols:\\n            df = df[df[cols[\'weight\']] > 0].copy()\\n        df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\\n        df[\'timestamp\'] = np.arange(len(df))\\n    else:\\n        raise ValueError(name)\\n\\n    df = df[[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\']].dropna().copy()\\n    df[\'user\'] = df[\'user\'].astype(str)\\n    df[\'item\'] = df[\'item\'].astype(str)\\n    return df\\n\\n\\ndef core_filter(df, user_col=\'user\', item_col=\'item\', min_core=5):\\n    changed = True\\n    while changed:\\n        changed = False\\n        ucnt = df[user_col].value_counts()\\n        icnt = df[item_col].value_counts()\\n        before = len(df)\\n        df = df[df[user_col].isin(ucnt[ucnt >= min_core].index) & df[item_col].isin(icnt[icnt >= min_core].index)].copy()\\n        if len(df) != before:\\n            changed = True\\n    return df\\n\\n\\ndef make_user_holdout(df, seed, frac=0.2):\\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n    test_idx = []\\n    for u, g in df.groupby(\'user\').groups.items():\\n        idx = np.array(list(g))\\n        ntest = max(1, int(np.ceil(len(idx) * frac)))\\n        sel = rng.choice(idx, size=min(ntest, len(idx)-1) if len(idx) > 1 else 1, replace=False)\\n        test_idx.extend(sel.tolist())\\n    test = df.loc[test_idx].copy()\\n    train = df.drop(index=test_idx).copy()\\n    return train, test\\n\\n\\ndef build_relevance(train, test):\\n    rel = defaultdict(set)\\n    for u, i in test[[\'user\', \'item\']].itertuples(index=False):\\n        rel[u].add(i)\\n    users = [u for u in rel.keys() if u in set(train[\'user\'])]\\n    return rel, users\\n\\n\\ndef eval_rankings(recs, rel, users, ks):\\n    rows = []\\n    rec_map = {u: grp[\'item\'].tolist() for u, grp in recs.groupby(\'user\')}\\n    for k in ks:\\n        ndcgs, precs = [], []\\n        for u in users:\\n            rec_items = rec_map.get(u, [])[:k]\\n            gt = rel[u]\\n            y_true = np.array([1 if x in gt else 0 for x in rec_items], dtype=float)\\n            if len(y_true) == 0:\\n                ndcgs.append(0.0); precs.append(0.0); continue\\n            ndcgs.append(float(ndcg_score([y_true], [np.arange(len(y_true), 0, -1)])))\\n            precs.append(float(y_true.mean()))\\n        rows.append({\'k\': k, \'ndcg\': float(np.mean(ndcgs)), \'precision\': float(np.mean(precs))})\\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\\n\\n\\ndef run_algo(name, train):\\n    if name == \'ALS\':\\n        model = BiasedMF(features=20, iterations=15, reg=0.1, damping=10)\\n    elif name == \'ItemKNN\':\\n        model = ItemItem(nnbrs=40, min_nbrs=1, center=False)\\n    elif name == \'Pop\':\\n        model = Popular()\\n    else:\\n        raise ValueError(name)\\n    model.fit(train)\\n    return model\\n\\n# -----------------------\\n# Experiment\\n# -----------------------\\nsummary_rows = []\\nfor dname, cfg in datasets.items():\\n    print(f\'Loading {dname}...\')\\n    df = load_dataset(dname, cfg)\\n    df = core_filter(df, min_core=5)\\n    df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\\n    df = df[[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\']].drop_duplicates()\\n    print(f\'{dname}: {len(df)} interactions, {df.user.nunique()} users, {df.item.nunique()} items\')\\n\\n    for seed in seeds:\\n        train, test = make_user_holdout(df, seed)\\n        rel, users = build_relevance(train, test)\\n        if len(users) == 0:\\n            continue\\n        for algo in alg_names:\\n            print(f\'Training {dname} | seed={seed} | {algo}\')\\n            model = run_algo(algo, train)\\n            recs = recommend(model, users, 10)\\n            metric_df = eval_rankings(recs, rel, users, ks)\\n            for _, r in metric_df.iterrows():\\n                summary_rows.append({\'dataset\': dname, \'seed\': seed, \'algo\': algo, \'k\': int(r[\'k\']), \'ndcg\': r[\'ndcg\'], \'precision\': r[\'precision\']})\\n            experiment_data[dname][\'per_seed\'].append({\'seed\': seed, \'algo\': algo, \'metrics\': metric_df.to_dict(\'records\')})\\n            experiment_data[dname][\'metrics\'][\'ndcg\'].append(metric_df[[\'k\', \'ndcg\']].to_numpy())\\n            experiment_data[dname][\'metrics\'][\'precision\'].append(metric_df[[\'k\', \'precision\']].to_numpy())\\n            experiment_data[dname][\'predictions\'].append(recs.head(50).to_numpy())\\n            experiment_data[dname][\'ground_truth\'].append(test[[\'user\', \'item\']].head(50).to_numpy())\\n            experiment_data[dname][\'losses\'][\'train\'].append(np.nan)\\n            experiment_data[dname][\'losses\'][\'val\'].append(np.nan)\\n            print(f\'Epoch 1: validation_loss = {np.nan:.4f}\')\\n\\nsummary = pd.DataFrame(summary_rows)\\nsummary.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, \'summary_metrics.csv\'), index=False)\\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'experiment_data.npy\'), experiment_data, allow_pickle=True)\\n\\n# -----------------------\\n# Statistical analysis\\n# -----------------------\\nstat_rows = []\\nfor dname in summary[\'dataset\'].unique():\\n    for k in ks:\\n        sub = summary[(summary[\'dataset\'] == dname) & (summary[\'k\'] == k)]\\n        for metric in [\'ndcg\', \'precision\']:\\n            pivot = sub.pivot(index=\'see