[2026/05/15 20:57:32] [DEBUG] isgsa.llm: prompt content: {'Introduction': 'You are an experienced recommender systems researcher. Your previous code for research experiment had a bug, so based on the information below, you should revise it in order to fix this bug. Your response should be an implementation outline in natural language, followed by a single markdown code block which implements the bugfix/solution.', 'Research task': ' You are an expert recommender systems research assistant who is looking to help the user with their requests.\nThe user has some idea and you want to conduct creative experiments to gain scientific insights.\nYour aim is to run experiments to gather sufficient results to report back to the user.\nThe idea is:\n\nI’d like to run an experiment to quantify how much data split random seeds affect recommender system accuracy. Please use LensKit 0.14.4 to test three algorithms: ALS,\nItemKNN, and Pop. Run this on the following three datasets with implicit feedback:\nMovieLens100K, Amazon Video Games, Last.FM. The raw files are stored in your\nworking directory with the filenames u.data, VideoGames.csv, user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat. First, preprocess all datasets with 5-core filtering. For the Amazon\nand MovieLens datasets, please also convert any ratings greater than 3 to implicit\ninteractions. Here’s the main experimental procedure: Generate 5 different random\nseeds for data splitting. For each algorithm, dataset, and seed, please do a user-based\n80/20 holdout split. Train all models using standard hyperparameters. For the analysis, I need you to measure nDCG@k and Precision@k for k=1, 5, 10 and conduct a\nshort statistical analysis.', 'Previous (buggy) implementation': "```python\nimport os\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'working')\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom scipy import stats\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom sklearn.metrics import ndcg_score\n\nimport lenskit\nfrom lenskit.data import SparseMatrix\nfrom lenskit.batch import recommend\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import BiasedMF\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemItem\n\n# -----------------------\n# Config\n# -----------------------\nseeds = [11, 22, 33, 44, 55]\nks = [1, 5, 10]\ndatasets = {\n    'MovieLens100K': {'path': 'u.data', 'sep': '\\t', 'names': ['user', 'item', 'rating', 'timestamp'], 'movie': True},\n    'AmazonVideoGames': {'path': 'VideoGames.csv', 'sep': ',', 'names': None, 'movie': False},\n    'LastFM': {'path': 'user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat', 'sep': '\\t', 'names': None, 'movie': False},\n}\nalg_names = ['ALS', 'ItemKNN', 'Pop']\n\nexperiment_data = {}\nfor d in datasets:\n    experiment_data[d] = {\n        'metrics': {'ndcg': [], 'precision': []},\n        'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []},\n        'predictions': [],\n        'ground_truth': [],\n        'per_seed': [],\n    }\n\n# -----------------------\n# Helpers\n# -----------------------\ndef load_dataset(name, cfg):\n    p = cfg['path']\n    if not os.path.exists(p):\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f'Missing {p}')\n    if name == 'MovieLens100K':\n        df = pd.read_csv(p, sep='\\t', names=['user', 'item', 'rating', 'timestamp'], engine='python')\n        df = df[df['rating'] > 3].copy()\n        df['rating'] = 1.0\n    elif name == 'AmazonVideoGames':\n        df = pd.read_csv(p)\n        cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n        ucol = cols.get('user_id') or cols.get('reviewerid') or cols.get('user')\n        icol = cols.get('item_id') or cols.get('asin') or cols.get('item')\n        rcol = cols.get('rating') or cols.get('overall')\n        if ucol is None or icol is None:\n            raise ValueError('Could not identify user/item columns in Amazon data')\n        if rcol is None:\n            df['rating'] = 1.0\n        else:\n            df = df[df[rcol] > 3].copy()\n            df['rating'] = 1.0\n        df = df.rename(columns={ucol: 'user', icol: 'item'})\n        df['timestamp'] = np.arange(len(df))\n    elif name == 'LastFM':\n        df = pd.read_csv(p, sep='\\t')\n        cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n        ucol = cols.get('user_id') or cols.get('user')\n        icol = cols.get('artist_id') or cols.get('item_id') or cols.get('artist')\n        if ucol is None or icol is None:\n            raise ValueError('Could not identify user/item columns in LastFM data')\n        df = df.rename(columns={ucol: 'user', icol: 'item'})\n        if 'weight' in cols:\n            df = df[df[cols['weight']] > 0].copy()\n        df['rating'] = 1.0\n        df['timestamp'] = np.arange(len(df))\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(name)\n\n    df = df[['user', 'item', 'rating']].dropna().copy()\n    df['user'] = df['user'].astype(str)\n    df['item'] = df['item'].astype(str)\n    return df\n\n\ndef core_filter(df, user_col='user', item_col='item', min_core=5):\n    changed = True\n    while changed:\n        changed = False\n        ucnt = df[user_col].value_counts()\n        icnt = df[item_col].value_counts()\n        before = len(df)\n        df = df[df[user_col].isin(ucnt[ucnt >= min_core].index) & df[item_col].isin(icnt[icnt >= min_core].index)].copy()\n        if len(df) != before:\n            changed = True\n    return df\n\n\ndef make_user_holdout(df, seed, frac=0.2):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    test_idx = []\n    for u, g in df.groupby('user').groups.items():\n        idx = np.array(list(g))\n        ntest = max(1, int(np.ceil(len(idx) * frac)))\n        sel = rng.choice(idx, size=min(ntest, len(idx)-1) if len(idx) > 1 else 1, replace=False)\n        test_idx.extend(sel.tolist())\n    test = df.loc[test_idx].copy()\n    train = df.drop(index=test_idx).copy()\n    return train, test\n\n\ndef build_relevance(train, test):\n    rel = defaultdict(set)\n    for u, i in test[['user', 'item']].itertuples(index=False):\n        rel[u].add(i)\n    users = [u for u in rel.keys() if u in set(train['user'])]\n    return rel, users\n\n\ndef eval_rankings(recs, rel, users, ks):\n    rows = []\n    rec_map = {u: grp['item'].tolist() for u, grp in recs.groupby('user')}\n    for k in ks:\n        ndcgs, precs = [], []\n        for u in users:\n            rec_items = rec_map.get(u, [])[:k]\n            gt = rel[u]\n            y_true = np.array([1 if x in gt else 0 for x in rec_items], dtype=float)\n            if len(y_true) == 0:\n                ndcgs.append(0.0); precs.append(0.0); continue\n            ndcgs.append(float(ndcg_score([y_true], [np.arange(len(y_true), 0, -1)])))\n            precs.append(float(y_true.mean()))\n        rows.append({'k': k, 'ndcg': float(np.mean(ndcgs)), 'precision': float(np.mean(precs))})\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\n\ndef run_algo(name, train):\n    if name == 'ALS':\n        model = BiasedMF(features=20, iterations=15, reg=0.1, damping=10)\n    elif name == 'ItemKNN':\n        model = ItemItem(nnbrs=40, min_nbrs=1, center=False)\n    elif name == 'Pop':\n        model = Popular()\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(name)\n    model.fit(train)\n    return model\n\n# -----------------------\n# Experiment\n# -----------------------\nsummary_rows = []\nfor dname, cfg in datasets.items():\n    print(f'Loading {dname}...')\n    df = load_dataset(dname, cfg)\n    df = core_filter(df, min_core=5)\n    df['rating'] = 1.0\n    df = df[['user', 'item', 'rating']].drop_duplicates()\n    print(f'{dname}: {len(df)} interactions, {df.user.nunique()} users, {df.item.nunique()} items')\n\n    for seed in seeds:\n        train, test = make_user_holdout(df, seed)\n        rel, users = build_relevance(train, test)\n        if len(users) == 0:\n            continue\n        for algo in alg_names:\n            print(f'Training {dname} | seed={seed} | {algo}')\n            model = run_algo(algo, train)\n            recs = recommend(model, users, 10)\n            metric_df = eval_rankings(recs, rel, users, ks)\n            for _, r in metric_df.iterrows():\n                summary_rows.append({'dataset': dname, 'seed': seed, 'algo': algo, 'k': int(r['k']), 'ndcg': r['ndcg'], 'precision': r['precision']})\n            experiment_data[dname]['per_seed'].append({'seed': seed, 'algo': algo, 'metrics': metric_df.to_dict('records')})\n            experiment_data[dname]['metrics']['ndcg'].append(metric_df[['k', 'ndcg']].to_numpy())\n            experiment_data[dname]['metrics']['precision'].append(metric_df[['k', 'precision']].to_numpy())\n            experiment_data[dname]['predictions'].append(recs.head(50).to_numpy())\n            experiment_data[dname]['ground_truth'].append(test[['user', 'item']].head(50).to_numpy())\n            experiment_data[dname]['losses']['train'].append(np.nan)\n            experiment_data[dname]['losses']['val'].append(np.nan)\n            print(f'Epoch 1: validation_loss = {np.nan:.4f}')\n\nsummary = pd.DataFrame(summary_rows)\nsummary.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, 'summary_metrics.csv'), index=False)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'experiment_data.npy'), experiment_data, allow_pickle=True)\n\n# -----------------------\n# Statistical analysis\n# -----------------------\nstat_rows = []\nfor dname in summary['dataset'].unique():\n    for k in ks:\n        sub = summary[(summary['dataset'] == dname) & (summary['k'] == k)]\n        for metric in ['ndcg', 'precision']:\n            pivot = sub.pivot(index='seed', columns='algo', values=metric)\n            algs = pivot.columns.tolist()\n            for i in range(len(algs)):\n                for j in range(i + 1, len(algs)):\n                    x = pivot[algs[i]].values\n                    y = pivot[algs[j]].values\n                    if np.all(np.isfinite(x)) and np.all(np.isfinite(y)) and len(x) > 1:\n                        t = stats.ttest_rel(x, y, nan_policy='omit')\n                        stat_rows.append({'dataset': dname, 'k': k, 'metric': metric, 'a': algs[i], 'b': algs[j], 't': float(t.statistic), 'p': float(t.pvalue)})\n\nstat_df = pd.DataFrame(stat_rows)\nstat_df.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, 'stat_tests.csv'), index=False)\n\n# Print concise results\nprint('\\n=== Mean±Std over seeds ===')\nprint(summary.groupby(['dataset', 'algo', 'k'])[['ndcg', 'precision']].agg(['mean', 'std']).round(4))\nprint('\\n=== Paired t-tests ===')\nprint(stat_df.round(4) if len(stat_df) else 'No valid paired tests computed.')\n\n```", 'Execution output': '```\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File "C:\\Users\\lukas\\AutoRecLab_Team7\\treesearch\\interpreter.py", line 147, in _run_session\n    exec(compile(code, self.agent_file_name, "exec"), global_scope)\n  File "runfile.py", line 15, in <module>\nImportError: cannot import name \'SparseMatrix\' from \'lenskit.data\' (C:\\Users\\lukas\\AutoRecLab_Team7\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\lenskit\\data\\__init__.py)\nExecution time: a second seconds (time limit is an hour).\n```', 'Bug Analysis & Scoring': "\n                Bug Analysis:\n                Execution failed immediately with an ImportError: `cannot import name 'SparseMatrix' from 'lenskit.data'`. This prevents the experiment from running at all. Fix by removing the unused `SparseMatrix` import or updating it to a valid LensKit 0.14.4 import path/API. After that, verify the rest of the LensKit API calls (`BiasedMF`, `Popular`, `ItemItem`, and `recommend`) match version 0.14.4, since additional compatibility issues may remain.\n\n                This indicates the code failed to execute properly. Focus on addressing the specific error mentioned above.\n                \n                Previous Implementation Scores:\n                - Score: 0.0%\n                - Is Satisfactory: False\n                - Feedback: EXECUTION FAILURE DETECTED:\n\n                    Execution failed immediately with an ImportError: `cannot import name 'SparseMatrix' from 'lenskit.data'`. This prevents t