[2026/05/15 21:00:56] [DEBUG] isgsa.llm: prompt content: {'Introduction': 'You are an experienced recommender systems researcher. Your previous code for research experiment had a bug, so based on the information below, you should revise it in order to fix this bug. Your response should be an implementation outline in natural language, followed by a single markdown code block which implements the bugfix/solution.', 'Research task': ' You are an expert recommender systems research assistant who is looking to help the user with their requests.\nThe user has some idea and you want to conduct creative experiments to gain scientific insights.\nYour aim is to run experiments to gather sufficient results to report back to the user.\nThe idea is:\n\nI’d like to run an experiment to quantify how much data split random seeds affect recommender system accuracy. Please use LensKit 0.14.4 to test three algorithms: ALS,\nItemKNN, and Pop. Run this on the following three datasets with implicit feedback:\nMovieLens100K, Amazon Video Games, Last.FM. The raw files are stored in your\nworking directory with the filenames u.data, VideoGames.csv, user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat. First, preprocess all datasets with 5-core filtering. For the Amazon\nand MovieLens datasets, please also convert any ratings greater than 3 to implicit\ninteractions. Here’s the main experimental procedure: Generate 5 different random\nseeds for data splitting. For each algorithm, dataset, and seed, please do a user-based\n80/20 holdout split. Train all models using standard hyperparameters. For the analysis, I need you to measure nDCG@k and Precision@k for k=1, 5, 10 and conduct a\nshort statistical analysis.', 'Previous (buggy) implementation': "```python\nimport os\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'working')\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nimport re\nimport math\nimport json\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom scipy import stats\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n# LensKit 0.14.4 imports\nfrom lenskit import topn, batch\nfrom lenskit.algorithms import als, basic\n\nnp.random.seed(42)\n\nexperiment_data = {\n    'MovieLens100K': {'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'predictions': [], 'ground_truth': []},\n    'AmazonVideoGames': {'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'predictions': [], 'ground_truth': []},\n    'LastFM': {'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'predictions': [], 'ground_truth': []},\n}\n\nDATASETS = {\n    'MovieLens100K': {'path': os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'u.data'), 'sep': '\\t', 'columns': ['user', 'item', 'rating', 'timestamp'], 'kind': 'movielens'},\n    'AmazonVideoGames': {'path': os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'VideoGames.csv'), 'sep': ',', 'columns': None, 'kind': 'amazon'},\n    'LastFM': {'path': os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat'), 'sep': '\\t', 'columns': None, 'kind': 'lastfm'},\n}\nSEEDS = [11, 22, 33, 44, 55]\nKS = [1, 5, 10]\nALGO_NAMES = ['ALS', 'ItemKNN', 'Pop']\n\ndef _standardize_cols(df):\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n    return cols\n\ndef load_dataset(name, meta):\n    p = meta['path']\n    if name == 'MovieLens100K':\n        df = pd.read_csv(p, sep='\\t', header=None, names=['user', 'item', 'rating', 'timestamp'])\n        df = df[df['rating'] > 3].copy()\n    elif name == 'AmazonVideoGames':\n        df = pd.read_csv(p)\n        cols = _standardize_cols(df)\n        user_col = cols.get('reviewerid') or cols.get('user_id') or cols.get('reviewer_id') or list(df.columns)[0]\n        item_col = cols.get('asin') or cols.get('item_id') or list(df.columns)[1]\n        rating_col = cols.get('overall') or cols.get('rating') or list(df.columns)[2]\n        df = df[[user_col, item_col, rating_col]].copy()\n        df.columns = ['user', 'item', 'rating']\n        df = df[df['rating'] > 3].copy()\n    elif name == 'LastFM':\n        df = pd.read_csv(p, sep='\\t')\n        cols = _standardize_cols(df)\n        user_col = cols.get('userID'.lower()) or cols.get('user') or list(df.columns)[0]\n        item_col = cols.get('artistid'.lower()) or cols.get('artist_id') or cols.get('artist') or list(df.columns)[1]\n        df = df[[user_col, item_col]].copy()\n        df.columns = ['user', 'item']\n        df['rating'] = 1.0\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(name)\n    df = df[['user', 'item', 'rating']].copy()\n    df['user'] = df['user'].astype(str)\n    df['item'] = df['item'].astype(str)\n    if 'rating' not in df:\n        df['rating'] = 1.0\n    df = df.groupby(['user', 'item'], as_index=False)['rating'].max()\n    return df\n\ndef core_filter(df, min_uc=5, min_ic=5):\n    changed = True\n    while changed:\n        changed = False\n        ucounts = df.groupby('user').size()\n        keep_u = ucounts[ucounts >= min_uc].index\n        df2 = df[df['user'].isin(keep_u)]\n        icounts = df2.groupby('item').size()\n        keep_i = icounts[icounts >= min_ic].index\n        df3 = df2[df2['item'].isin(keep_i)]\n        if len(df3) != len(df):\n            changed = True\n        df = df3\n    return df.reset_index(drop=True)\n\ndef user_holdout_split(df, seed, frac=0.2):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    train_parts = []\n    test_parts = []\n    for u, g in df.groupby('user'):\n        idx = g.index.to_numpy()\n        n_test = max(1, int(round(len(idx) * frac)))\n        test_idx = rng.choice(idx, size=n_test, replace=False)\n        train_idx = np.setdiff1d(idx, test_idx)\n        if len(train_idx) == 0:\n            train_idx, test_idx = idx[:1], idx[1:]\n        train_parts.append(df.loc[train_idx])\n        test_parts.append(df.loc[test_idx])\n    train = pd.concat(train_parts, ignore_index=True)\n    test = pd.concat(test_parts, ignore_index=True)\n    return train, test\n\ndef make_topn_lists(train, test, algo, kmax=10):\n    train_ui = train[['user', 'item']].copy()\n    test_ui = test[['user', 'item']].copy()\n    reco = topn.recommend(algo, train_ui, users=test_ui['user'].unique(), k=kmax, exclude_known=True)\n    return reco, test_ui\n\ndef eval_metrics(reco, test, ks=(1, 5, 10)):\n    gt = test.groupby('user')['item'].apply(list).to_dict()\n    reco = reco.copy()\n    reco['rank'] = reco.groupby('user').cumcount() + 1\n    out = {}\n    for k in ks:\n        precs, ndcgs = [], []\n        for u, true_items in gt.items():\n            user_rec = reco[(reco['user'] == u) & (reco['rank'] <= k)]['item'].tolist()\n            hits = [1 if i in true_items else 0 for i in user_rec]\n            precs.append(sum(hits) / k)\n            dcg = sum(h / math.log2(r + 2) for r, h in enumerate(hits))\n            ideal = min(len(true_items), k)\n            idcg = sum(1.0 / math.log2(r + 2) for r in range(ideal)) if ideal > 0 else 1.0\n            ndcgs.append(dcg / idcg if idcg > 0 else 0.0)\n        out[f'precision@{k}'] = float(np.mean(precs))\n        out[f'ndcg@{k}'] = float(np.mean(ndcgs))\n    return out\n\ndef build_algorithms(train):\n    items = train['item'].unique()\n    item_pop = basic.PopularityRecommender()\n    item_knn = basic.ItemItem(20)\n    als_model = als.BiasedMF(features=20, iterations=15, reg=0.1)\n    return {'Pop': item_pop, 'ItemKNN': item_knn, 'ALS': als_model}\n\ndef fit_predict(algo, train, test_users):\n    algo.fit(train[['user', 'item']])\n    recs = topn.recommend(algo, train[['user', 'item']], users=test_users, k=10, exclude_known=True)\n    return recs\n\nall_results = []\nfor ds_name, meta in DATASETS.items():\n    print(f'Loading {ds_name}...')\n    df = load_dataset(ds_name, meta)\n    df = core_filter(df, 5, 5)\n    print(f'{ds_name}: {len(df)} interactions, {df.user.nunique()} users, {df.item.nunique()} items')\n    for seed in SEEDS:\n        train, test = user_holdout_split(df, seed=seed, frac=0.2)\n        test_users = test['user'].unique()\n        algos = build_algorithms(train)\n        for algo_name, algo in algos.items():\n            recs = fit_predict(algo, train, test_users)\n            metrics = eval_metrics(recs, test, ks=KS)\n            row = {'dataset': ds_name, 'seed': seed, 'algorithm': algo_name}\n            row.update(metrics)\n            all_results.append(row)\n            experiment_data[ds_name]['metrics']['val'].append(row)\n            experiment_data[ds_name]['predictions'].append(recs[['user', 'item', 'rank']].to_numpy())\n            experiment_data[ds_name]['ground_truth'].append(test[['user', 'item']].to_numpy())\n            print(ds_name, seed, algo_name, metrics)\n\nresults = pd.DataFrame(all_results)\nprint('\\nAggregate results (mean ± std over seeds):')\nsummary = results.groupby(['dataset', 'algorithm']).agg(['mean', 'std'])\nprint(summary)\n\nstat_rows = []\nfor ds in results['dataset'].unique():\n    print(f'\\nStatistical comparison on {ds}:')\n    sub = results[results['dataset'] == ds]\n    pivot = sub.pivot(index='seed', columns='algorithm')\n    for metric in [f'precision@{k}' for k in KS] + [f'ndcg@{k}' for k in KS]:\n        vals = pivot[metric]\n        for a1 in ALGO_NAMES:\n            for a2 in ALGO_NAMES:\n                if a1 >= a2:\n                    continue\n                x = vals[a1].dropna().values\n                y = vals[a2].dropna().values\n                if len(x) == len(y) and len(x) > 1:\n                    t, p = stats.ttest_rel(x, y)\n                    stat_rows.append([ds, metric, a1, a2, float(t), float(p)])\n                    print(f'{metric}: {a1} vs {a2} paired t-test p={p:.4g}')\n\nstat_df = pd.DataFrame(stat_rows, columns=['dataset', 'metric', 'algo1', 'algo2', 't', 'p'])\nresults.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, 'seed_level_results.csv'), index=False)\nstat_df.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, 'stat_tests.csv'), index=False)\n\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'experiment_data.npy'), experiment_data)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'results_array.npy'), results.to_numpy())\n\nfor ds in results['dataset'].unique():\n    sub = results[results['dataset'] == ds]\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(14, 7), constrained_layout=True)\n    for j, metric in enumerate([f'precision@{k}' for k in KS] + [f'ndcg@{k}' for k in KS]):\n        ax = axes.flat[j]\n        for algo in ALGO_NAMES:\n            vals = sub[sub['algorithm'] == algo].sort_values('seed')[metric].values\n            ax.plot(SEEDS, vals, marker='o', label=algo)\n        ax.set_title(f'{ds} - {metric}')\n        ax.set_xlabel('seed')\n        ax.set_ylabel(metric)\n        ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n    axes.flat[0].legend()\n    fig_path = os.path.join(working_dir, f'{ds}_seed_sensitivity.png')\n    plt.savefig(fig_path, dpi=150)\n    plt.close(fig)\n\nprint('\\nSaved outputs to:', working_dir)\nprint(results.head())\n\n```", 'Execution output': '```\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File "C:\\Users\\lukas\\AutoRecLab_Team7\\treesearch\\interpreter.py", line 147, in _run_session\n    exec(compile(code, self.agent_file_name, "exec"), global_scope)\n  File "runfile.py", line 10, in <module>\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named \'matplotlib\'\nExecution time: a moment seconds (time limit is an hour).\n```', 'Bug Analysis & Scoring': "\n                Bug Analysis:\n                Execution failed immediately with ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'matplotlib' during imports, so none of the recommender experiments or metrics were produced. Fix by installing matplotlib in the environment or removing the plotting dependency if plots are optional. After that, verify LensKit 0.14.4 API compatibility as there may be additional runtime issues later in the script.\n\n                This indicates the code failed to execute properly. Focus on addressing the specific error mentioned above.\n                \n                Previous Implementation Scores:\n                - Score: 0.0%\n                - Is Satisfactory: False\n                - Feedback: EXECUTION FAILU